---
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import ScrollTable from '../../components/ScrollTable.astro';
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import { ICON_AXES_DEMO as demo } from '../../data/icon-demo';
// The site's icon font pins the weight; the demo's weight row uses this face (scripts/icons.js).
import '../../generated/icons/site-icons-axes.css';

const profiles = [
  { entry: 'fonts.css', axes: 'wght, opsz (default)', latin: '138.8 KiB', all: '328.5 KiB' },
  { entry: 'fonts-rond.css', axes: 'wght, opsz, ROND', latin: '205.2 KiB', all: '468.1 KiB' },
  { entry: 'fonts-full.css', axes: 'wght, opsz, ROND, wdth, slnt', latin: '1020.8 KiB', all: '2026.8 KiB' },
];
---

<Guide
  title="Fonts and icons"
  description="Google Sans Flex, the variable typeface of M3 Expressive, ships with the tokens in three profiles; icons are Material Symbols ligatures you can subset to the glyphs you use."
>
  <h2 id="font">Google Sans Flex</h2>
  <p>
    The type scale is set in Google Sans Flex, self-hosted from <code>@kyralabs/m3e-tokens</code>
    (DECISIONS D1, D11). Pick one profile: each registers the same
    <code>"Google Sans Flex"</code> family, so they replace each other instead of adding up.
    Browsers download only the chunks a page's text needs.
  </p>
  <ScrollTable label="Font profiles">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Entry</th><th scope="col">Variable axes</th><th scope="col">Latin chunk</th><th scope="col">All chunks</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          profiles.map((p) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><code>{p.entry}</code></th>
              <td>{p.axes}</td>
              <td>{p.latin}</td>
              <td>{p.all}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </ScrollTable>
  <p>
    <code>@kyralabs/m3exp-web/css/index.css</code> includes <code>fonts.css</code>. The type scale
    uses weight only (emphasized styles are heavier) and drives optical size from the font size
    with <code>font-optical-sizing: auto</code>; axes a profile drops stay at their defaults, so
    every profile renders the type scale identically.
  </p>
  <h3 id="other-profiles">Use another profile</h3>
  <p>
    Import the profile with the token and theme stylesheets and the component classes, in place of
    <code>css/index.css</code>:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    lang="css"
    label="roundness profile imports"
    code={`@import '@kyralabs/m3e-tokens/fonts-rond.css'; /* instead of fonts.css */
@import '@kyralabs/m3e-tokens/tokens.css';
@import '@kyralabs/m3e-tokens/theme.css';
@import '@kyralabs/m3e-css/index.css';`}
  />
  <p>
    Roundness (<code>ROND</code>, 0 to 100) has no CSS property of its own; set it with
    <code>font-variation-settings</code>. That property replaces any value it inherits instead of
    merging with it, so repeat the other axes you set in the same declaration. No Material source
    gives roundness values for the type scale, so the tokens never set it.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    lang="css"
    label="roundness example"
    code={`.playful {
  font-variation-settings: 'ROND' 100;
}`}
  />
  <p>
    The fonts ship with their licenses beside them in <code>@kyralabs/m3e-tokens/fonts/</code>:
    Google Sans Flex under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, Material Symbols under Apache 2.0.
    "Google Sans" is a trademark of Google LLC.
  </p>

  <h2 id="icons">Material Symbols</h2>
  <p>
    Icons are Material Symbols ligatures (DECISIONS D5): the icon's name, set in the icon font.
    The default style is Rounded (D12); Outlined and Sharp ship as their own stylesheets. Load one:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    lang="css"
    label="icon stylesheet imports"
    code={`@import '@kyralabs/m3e-tokens/material-symbols.css'; /* Rounded */
/* or material-symbols-outlined.css, material-symbols-sharp.css */`}
  />
  <p>Every layer renders the same <code>.m3e-icon</code> span:</p>
  <CodeBlock
    lang="html"
    label="icon markup"
    code={`<span class="m3e-icon" aria-hidden="true">favorite</span>
<span class="m3e-icon" aria-hidden="true" data-fill>favorite</span>

<m3e-icon name="favorite" fill weight="500"></m3e-icon>`}
  />
  <CodeBlock
    lang="tsx"
    label="React icon"
    code={`import { Icon } from '@kyralabs/m3exp-web/react';

<Icon name="favorite" fill weight={500} grade={-25} opticalSize={20} />
<Icon name="info" label="Information" /> {/* role="img" with a name */}`}
  />
  <p>
    Icons are decorative by default (<code>aria-hidden</code>); give an icon that stands alone a
    label, or name the control around it. Selected states fill their icon
    (<code>FILL</code> 1). The axes come from tokens and can be set per icon with
    <code>--m3e-comp-icon-fill</code>, <code>--m3e-comp-icon-weight</code>,
    <code>--m3e-comp-icon-grade</code>, <code>--m3e-comp-icon-optical-size</code>, and the size
    with <code>--m3e-comp-icon-size</code>.
  </p>
  <figure class="site-icon-demo">
    <div class="site-icon-demo__row">
      {demo.map((name) => <span class="m3e-icon" aria-hidden="true">{name}</span>)}
    </div>
    <div class="site-icon-demo__row">
      {demo.map((name) => <span class="m3e-icon" aria-hidden="true" data-fill>{name}</span>)}
    </div>
    <div class="site-icon-demo__row site-icon-demo__row--bold site-icon-demo__row--axes">
      {demo.map((name) => <span class="m3e-icon" aria-hidden="true">{name}</span>)}
    </div>
    <figcaption>Rounded icons: default, filled, and weight 700.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h3 id="subset">Ship only your icons</h3>
  <p>
    The full variable fonts weigh several megabytes (Rounded: about 5 MB). The
    <code>m3e-icons</code> CLI subsets one to the names you list and writes a drop-in
    <code>@font-face</code> stylesheet that points <code>.m3e-icon</code> at it:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    lang="sh"
    label="subset commands"
    code={`npm install --save-dev @kyralabs/m3e-icons
npx m3e-icons subset --names home,search,menu --out public/icons.woff2 --css public/icons.css`}
  />
  <p>
    Load <code>icons.css</code> instead of <code>material-symbols.css</code>. Include the icons
    components draw on their own, such as the date picker's arrows or the search bar's back button.
    Options: <code>--names-file</code>, <code>--style rounded|outlined|sharp</code>, and
    <code>--fill</code>, <code>--wght</code>, <code>--grad</code>, <code>--opsz</code> to pin an
    axis or narrow its range for a smaller file. Build scripts can call the exported
    <code>subsetIcons()</code> instead.
  </p>
</Guide>
